    "created_at": "2015-12-11T16:38:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-11T16:38:57Z",
    "body": "This doesn't seem correct. We should be giving a normative list of what the possible supported tokens are. For example, \"tag\" is a HTML link type, but `a.supports(\"tag\")` should be false since it has no impact on processing.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
