    "body": "Merged as https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/399c565d4db8479a587014e9975e59cadb9fc110 with the following additional tweaks applied for the record:\n\n``` diff\ndiff --git a/source b/source\nindex 5558aaa..e722f00 100644\n--- a/source\n+++ b/source\n@@ -12045,13 +12045,14 @@ gave me some of the songs they wrote. I love sharing my music.&lt;/p>\n   <code data-x=\"rel-alternate\">alternate</code>, <code data-x=\"rel-icon\">icon</code>,\n   <code data-x=\"rel-pingback\">pingback</code>, <code data-x=\"rel-prefetch\">prefetch</code>,\n   <code data-x=\"rel-stylesheet\">stylesheet</code> and <code data-x=\"rel-next\">next</code>.\n-  <code data-x=\"dom-link-rel\">rel</code>'s\n+  <code data-x=\"attr-link-rel\">rel</code>'s\n   <span data-x=\"concept-supported-tokens\">supported tokens</span> must only include the tokens from\n   this list that the user agent implements the processing model for.</p>\n\n   <p>Other specifications may add <a href=\"#linkTypes\">HTML link types</a> as\n   defined in <a href=\"#other-link-types\">Other link types</a>. These specifications may require\n-  that their link types be included in <code data-x=\"attr-link-rel\">rel</code>'s supported tokens.</p>\n+  that their link types be included in <code data-x=\"attr-link-rel\">rel</code>'s supported\n+  tokens.</p>\n\n   </div>\n\n@@ -20418,10 +20419,11 @@ document.body.appendChild(wbr);</pre>\n\n   <p><code data-x=\"attr-hyperlink-rel\">rel</code>'s\n   <span data-x=\"concept-supported-tokens\">supported tokens</span> are the keywords defined in\n-  <a href=\"#linkTypes\">HTML link types</a> which are allowed on <code>a</code> and <code>area</code> elements, impact\n-  the processing model, and are supported by the user agent. The possible supported tokens are\n+  <a href=\"#linkTypes\">HTML link types</a> which are allowed on <code>a</code> and\n+  <code>area</code> elements, impact the processing model, and are supported by the user agent. The\n+  possible supported tokens are\n   <code data-x=\"rel-noreferrer\">noreferrer</code>,\n-  <code data-x=\"rel-noopener\">noopener</code> and\n+  <code data-x=\"rel-noopener\">noopener</code>, and\n   <code data-x=\"rel-prefetch\">prefetch</code>.\n   <code data-x=\"attr-hyperlink-rel\">rel</code>'s\n   <span data-x=\"concept-supported-tokens\">supported tokens</span> must only include the tokens from\n@@ -20429,8 +20431,8 @@ document.body.appendChild(wbr);</pre>\n\n   <p>Other specifications may add <a href=\"#linkTypes\">HTML link types</a> as\n   defined in <a href=\"#other-link-types\">Other link types</a>. These specifications may require\n-  that their link types be included in <code data-x=\"attr-hyperlink-rel\">rel</code>'s supported tokens.\n-  </p>\n+  that their link types be included in <code data-x=\"attr-hyperlink-rel\">rel</code>'s supported\n+  tokens.</p>\n\n   <p>The <code data-x=\"attr-hyperlink-rel\">rel</code> attribute has no default value. If the\n   attribute is omitted or if none of the values in the attribute are recognised by the user agent,\n@@ -27089,9 +27091,8 @@ href=\"?audio\">audio&lt;/a> test instead.)&lt;/p></pre>\n   content attributes of the same name.</p>\n\n   <p>The <span data-x=\"concept-supported-tokens\">supported tokens</span> for <code\n-  data-x=\"dom-iframe-sandbox\">sandbox</code>'s <code>DOMSettableTokenList</code> are the allowed\n-  values defined in the <code data-x=\"attr-iframe-sandbox\">sandbox</code> attribute and supported by\n-  the user agent.</p>\n+  data-x=\"attr-iframe-sandbox\">sandbox</code> are the allowed values defined for the <code\n+  data-x=\"attr-iframe-sandbox\">sandbox</code> attribute that are supported by the user agent.</p>\n\n   <p>The <dfn><code data-x=\"dom-iframe-allowFullscreen\">allowFullscreen</code></dfn> IDL attribute\n   must <span>reflect</span> the <code data-x=\"attr-iframe-allowfullscreen\">allowfullscreen</code>\n@@ -77179,8 +77180,8 @@ dictionary <dfn>DragEventInit</dfn> : <span>MouseEventInit</span> {\n   <span>reflect</span> the content attribute of the same name.</p>\n\n   <p>The <span data-x=\"concept-supported-tokens\">supported tokens</span> for\n-  <code data-x=\"dom-dropzone\">dropzone</code> are the allowed values defined for the\n-  <code data-x=\"attr-dropzone\">dropzone</code> attribute and supported by the user agent.</p>\n+  <code data-x=\"attr-dropzone\">dropzone</code> are the allowed values defined for the\n+  <code data-x=\"attr-dropzone\">dropzone</code> attribute that are supported by the user agent.</p>\n\n   </div>\n```\n\nThanks for sticking with us through this long review!! I think this is a pretty nice feature and am glad it's all specced out now :)\n",
